meta {
  name: 3. Get Balance (A)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/wallet/balance
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Telegram-Init-Data: {{initData}}
}

docs {
  balance_stars_equivalent is a display-only estimate (floor division by
  the current star_to_toman_rate) — it's never used to decide whether a
  charge succeeds; every real charge is computed from the priced item's
  own price_stars instead.

  pending_toman is money User A has earned as a provider from chat
  requests that got paid, but hasn't received yet — it only moves into
  balance_toman once the paid-for chat session CLOSES and the
  chat_release_grace_hours window passes with nobody disputing it (see
  TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENTS.md section 10 — "pool idle"). Run Requests >
  "6. Pay For Request (B)", then Chat Sessions > close it, then come
  back here — this endpoint is also what actually triggers the
  grace-period release check (it's lazy, not a background job), so the
  pending amount won't move into balance_toman until you hit this
  endpoint again after the grace window has passed.
}
